#N canvas 40 40 1300 780 12;
#X text 20 10 FS play - first instruments. Turn DSP on \, then move. mmrl: tilt-pitched drone that swells when you rotate \, flick-to-pluck (tilt picks the note) \, and percussive hits on roll / chop / wave gestures (needs run_fs.py --gesture-library). mms (sensor fusion): point up for higher notes \, twist to open the drone's filter \, rotate to swell \, flick to pluck - a third up. mms sphere: point at notes placed around you (8 in a ring just above the horizon + 1 overhead) \, move to bring in overtones \; let your arm hang for silence. Click recenter while pointing where front should be (needs fs_cmd to reach the Pi - edit its IP if DHCP moved it). The mms drone starts off since it also maps pointing to pitch. To try it without the Pi: python tools/replay_osc.py --synthetic, f 130;
#X obj 20 90 fs_net 12345;
#X floatatom 120 120 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 20 160 fs_device mmrl E0:2D:64:47:02:F5;
#X obj 400 160 fs_device mms EC:47:49:CF:53:C4;
#X obj 20 300 fs_drone mmrl 45;
#X obj 160 300 fs_pluck mmrl 57;
#X obj 300 300 fs_hit mmrl roll 300;
#X obj 300 330 fs_hit mmrl chop 1200;
#X obj 300 360 fs_hit mmrl wave 600;
#X obj 600 300 fs_drone_point mms 49;
#X obj 760 300 fs_pluck_point mms 61;
